  "seed": 42,
  "series": "MONGODB SCHEMA DESIGN",
  "date": "07/09/2026",
  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Document Model Fundamentals",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "BSON Under The Hood",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "BSON = binary JSON, typed and length-prefixed",
            "Extra types: `ObjectId`, `Date`, `Decimal128`, `Binary`",
            "`Int32` and `Int64` are distinct — JSON has one number",
            "Collections hold documents; no table shape enforced"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Ceiling",
            "Value",
            "Why it bites"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Doc size",
              "16 MB",
              "kills unbounded embedding"
            ],
            [
              "Nest depth",
              "100",
              "painful to index or query"
            ],
            [
              "`_id`",
              "required",
              "immutable, auto-unique"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Flexible, Not Absent",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every app has a schema — it lives in app code",
            "Server enforces nothing until you ask it to",
            "`$jsonSchema` checks required, `bsonType`, ranges",
            "`validationAction: 'warn'` logs; `'error'` rejects"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.createCollection('users', {",
            "  validator: { $jsonSchema: {",
            "    required: ['email'],",
            "    properties: { age: { bsonType: 'int' } }",
            "  } }, validationAction: 'error' })"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Warn Before Error",
          "text": "Ship `validationAction: 'warn'` first — violations land in the log while old documents keep writing. Flip to `'error'` once the log goes quiet."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Store Together, Read Together",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Model for query patterns, not entity purity",
            "3NF is the wrong default — denormalize deliberately",
            "One document read = one seek, one page, no join",
            "That single fact is the whole case for embedding"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ _id: ObjectId('...'),",
            "  name: 'Ada',",
            "  addresses: [ { city: 'Dublin' } ], // array",
            "  created: ISODate('2026-09-07') }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Depth And Shape",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "100 levels of nesting is the hard cap",
            "Deep nesting resists both indexing and querying",
            "Subdocuments and arrays are first-class citizens",
            "No join table needed to hold a child list"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Working Set",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Working set = indexes + frequently read documents",
            "Bigger than RAM: WiredTiger thrashes, reads hit disk",
            "`ObjectId` embeds a 4-byte timestamp up front",
            "So sorting by `_id` ≈ sorting by insertion time"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Can I just use transactions?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Yes — v4.0 replica sets, v4.2 sharded, real ACID",
            "But they cost far more than one embedded write",
            "Escape hatch, never the default plan"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Document Model Fundamentals (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Answer These First",
          "items": [
            "Top 5 queries by frequency?",
            "Read/write ratio per collection?",
            "Cardinality of each relationship?",
            "Is the child ever queried alone?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Shapes",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "compare",
          "spec": {
            "left": {
              "title": "Embed",
              "items": [
                "child lives in parent",
                "1 round trip",
                "atomic single-doc write",
                "bounded arrays only"
              ]
            },
            "right": {
              "title": "Reference",
              "items": [
                "child stores parent `_id`",
                "`$lookup` or 2nd query",
                "small normalized docs",
                "growth without ceiling"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "When To Embed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Child is always read with the parent",
            "Child has no independent lifecycle",
            "Array is bounded and stays bounded",
            "Price: duplication, fatter docs, more bytes moved"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "When To Reference",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Child is queried on its own",
            "Child is large, or written far more than the parent",
            "Array grows without a ceiling",
            "Start denormalized; normalize under pressure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What Drives The Call"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Signal",
            "Leans embed",
            "Leans reference"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "one-to-few",
              "embed array",
              "—"
            ],
            [
              "one-to-many",
              "—",
              "child holds parent id"
            ],
            [
              "squillions",
              "impossible",
              "parent-ref only"
            ],
            [
              "read-heavy",
              "duplicate fields",
              "—"
            ],
            [
              "write-heavy",
              "—",
              "avoid update fan-out"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "$lookup Is Not Free",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Left outer join executed on the server",
            "Sharded: foreign collection unsharded before v5.1",
            "v5.1+ allows a sharded foreign side, with limits",
            "Budget it as expensive, not as convenience"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.posts.find({}, { comments: 0 })",
            "// skips array; full doc still read off disk",
            "db.posts.find({}, {",
            "  comments: { $slice: -10 } }) // last 10"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Operation",
            "Embedded",
            "Referenced"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Read parent+kids",
              "1 query, 1 doc",
              "`$lookup` or N+1"
            ],
            [
              "Update one child",
              "rewrite parent doc",
              "update small child"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Default Position",
          "text": "Prefer embedding until a named requirement forces a reference. Denormalized first, normalized under measured pressure."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Bounded Handful",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Under ~100 children, never growing unbounded",
            "Addresses, phone numbers, roles, tags",
            "Stored as an array of subdocuments on the parent"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ _id: 1, name: 'Ada', addresses: [",
            "  { label: 'home', city: 'Dublin' },",
            "  { label: 'work', city: 'Cork' } ] }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Embed vs Reference",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Matching Elements",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.people.find({'addresses.city':'Dublin'})",
            "// dot notation matches any one element",
            "db.people.find({ addresses: { $elemMatch:",
            "  { label:'home', city:'Dublin' } } })"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Two Conditions, One Element",
          "text": "`{'addresses.label':'home','addresses.city':'Cork'}` matches a doc where different elements satisfy each half. `$elemMatch` is the only cure."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Indexing An Array",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`createIndex({'addresses.city':1})` becomes multikey",
            "Multikey indexes every element of every array",
            "One compound index may include only ONE array field",
            "Two multikey paths in one index is an error"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Updating In Place"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.people.updateOne(",
            "  {'addresses.label':'home'},",
            "  {$set:{'addresses.$.city':'Galway'}})"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`$[]` updates every element of the array",
            "`$[tag]` plus `arrayFilters` updates matching ones",
            "`$push` adds, `$pull` removes by predicate",
            "`$addToSet` adds only if absent — all atomic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "$push: { scores: { $each: [9],",
            "  $sort: { v: -1 }, $slice: 10 } }",
            "// capped, sorted array in one atomic op"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "What You Give Up",
          "items": [
            "Children have no identity unless you add an `_id`",
            "No index of their own, no lifecycle of their own",
            "Children cannot be queried alone",
            "Every match hands back whole parent documents"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Hundreds To Thousands",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Too many to embed, still enumerable per parent",
            "Child documents carry the parent's `_id`",
            "Parent holds nothing at all about the children"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// products: { _id, name }",
            "// parts: { _id, name, qty, product_id }",
            "db.parts.find({product_id: id}) // no rewrite"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Inverse Variant",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Parent stores an array of child `_id`s",
            "Good when order matters or the list stays short",
            "`db.parts.find({_id:{$in:product.parts}})`",
            "Child-holds-id instead grows with no parent rewrite"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "compare",
          "spec": {
            "left": {
              "title": "parts: [ids]",
              "items": [
                "order preserved",
                "one `$in` fetch",
                "array can bloat"
              ]
            },
            "right": {
              "title": "part.product_id",
              "items": [
                "unbounded growth",
                "parent untouched",
                "needs an index"
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "One-to-Few: Embed The Array",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Index The Foreign Key",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.parts.createIndex({ product_id: 1 })",
            "// without it every lookup is a COLLSCAN"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Join Or Two Queries"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Two queries often beat `$lookup` outright",
            "The client round trip is cheap; join memory is not",
            "A sub-pipeline filters the joined side before it lands",
            "That also cuts the 16 MB result risk"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ $lookup: { from: 'parts',",
            "  localField: '_id',",
            "  foreignField: 'product_id',",
            "  as: 'parts' } }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Recursive Joins",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`$graphLookup` walks org charts and category trees",
            "`maxDepth` bounds the walk — memory-hungry regardless"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "No Safety Net",
          "items": [
            "Cascade deletes do not exist here",
            "Removing a parent leaves orphan children",
            "App cleanup, or a transaction covering both"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Axis",
            "Embedded",
            "Referenced"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Consistency",
              "copies go stale",
              "always current"
            ],
            [
              "Atomicity",
              "free, one doc",
              "txn, 60 s default"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Millions Per Parent",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Log lines, sensor readings, events, message history",
            "Embedding is dead: 16 MB cap plus rewrite cost",
            "Array of ids dies too — 1M ObjectIds = 12 MB of ids",
            "Only shape left: child holds `host_id` / `device_id`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// logs { _id, host_id, time, level, msg }",
            "db.logs.createIndex({ host_id: 1, time: -1 })",
            "db.logs.find({ host_id })",
            "  .sort({ time: -1 }).limit(100) // slice"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "ESR Ordering",
          "text": "Equality field first, then Sort, then Range. `{host_id:1, time:-1}` — flip the order and the index stops serving the sort."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Never Read It All",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Query the most recent slice, always bounded by `limit`",
            "Pair with bucketing to cut document count 10-100x"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Expiring Old Children",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.logs.createIndex({ time: 1 },",
            "  { expireAfterSeconds: 2592000 }) // 30d",
            "// background sweep runs every 60 s"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Purpose-Built Storage"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Capped: fixed size, insertion order, auto-overwrite",
            "But no deletes, no shard key, limited updates",
            "Time series (v5.0+): `timeField`, `metaField`, `granularity`",
            "You declare it; the server buckets internally"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Automatic columnar compression, clustered index on time",
            "Often 10x smaller than one document per reading"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "One-to-Many: Reference By Child",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Declaring It",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.createCollection('readings', {",
            "  timeseries: { timeField: 'ts',",
            "    metaField: 'sensor',",
            "    granularity: 'minutes' } })"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Sharding Decision",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A monotonic shard key (time) builds one hot chunk",
            "Use a compound or hashed key instead"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Hashed key scatters inserts across every chunk",
            "Compound key: `{ device_id: 1, time: 1 }`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Cardinality",
            "Shape"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "few (<100)",
              "embed array"
            ],
            [
              "many (100-10k)",
              "reference"
            ],
            [
              "squillions (>10k)",
              "parent-ref + bucket + TTL"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Trade Count For Size",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Group many small docs into one holding an array",
            "Per-doc overhead (BSON header, `_id`, index entry) dominates",
            "1M readings means 1M index entries and 1M seeks"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ _id, sensor_id, count: 60,",
            "  start: ISODate('..T10:00'), end: ...,",
            "  measurements: [ { t, v }, ... ] }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Choosing The Key",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Bucket key = entity plus window",
            "One per sensor per hour, one per user per day",
            "Or per device per 200 readings — count works too"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Filling A Bucket"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.b.updateOne(",
            "  { sensor_id, count: { $lt: 200 } },",
            "  { $push: { measurements: m },",
            "    $inc: { count: 1 } }, { upsert: true })"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Why The $lt Guard",
          "text": "The count predicate caps bucket size. When the current bucket fills it stops matching, and the upsert opens a fresh one on its own."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What You Gain",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Fewer index entries, far smaller index footprint",
            "Better locality: one disk read serves a whole window",
            "Precompute min, max, sum, count per bucket on write",
            "Dashboards read the rollup and never touch the array"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ sensor_id, start, count: 60,",
            "  min: 3.1, max: 9.4, sum: 372.0 }",
            "// dashboard reads this, not the array"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What You Pay",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Individual readings need `$unwind` or array filtering",
            "Ad-hoc single-reading lookups get awkward",
            "Size so a doc stays well under 16 MB, ideally a few hundred KB",
            "Oversized buckets punish the WiredTiger cache"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.b.find({ sensor_id,",
            "  start: { $gte: t0 }, end: { $lte: t1 } })",
            "// then $unwind + $match to drill in"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "The Bucket Pattern",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Reach Wider",
          "items": [
            "Cap by count OR window — time alone bounds nothing",
            "IoT batches, per-day chat transcripts",
            "Per-month invoice lines, page-view rollups",
            "v5.0+ time series does this natively; prefer it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "The Seek Math",
          "text": "A day of 1-minute data is 1440 document fetches, or 24 with hourly buckets. Same bytes, roughly 60x fewer seeks."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Compute On Write",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Calculate once at write, store it, read it free",
            "Trades write cost and staleness for read latency",
            "Three flavors: mathematical, roll-up, fan-out"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// product carries its own stats",
            "{ _id, name, review_count: 812,",
            "  rating_sum: 3492, rating_count: 812 }",
            "// avg derived, exact under concurrent $inc"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Beats running an aggregation on every page view",
            "Update atomically with `$inc` on the counter pair",
            "Sum + count is more robust than a stored average"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Extended Reference",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Copy the few displayed fields beside the reference id",
            "Order stores `{ customer_id, customer: { name, city } }`",
            "Rendering an order list then needs zero joins",
            "Copy `name` and `city`, never `last_login` or `balance`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Staleness Is The Bill",
          "text": "When the source changes you fan out updates, or accept eventual — sometimes never — consistency where it does no harm."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Keeping Copies Fresh",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Low-churn fields: synchronous fan-out on write is fine",
            "High-churn: a change stream or scheduled job instead",
            "`watch()` gives a resumable, ordered feed of changes",
            "That is the standard way to sync derived copies"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Subset Pattern"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Hot slice inline (top 10 reviews), full set elsewhere",
            "Bounds document size, keeps the common read one query"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Materialized Views",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.orders.aggregate([{ $group: {...} },",
            "  { $merge: { into: 'daily',",
            "    whenMatched: 'merge',",
            "    whenNotMatched: 'insert' } } ])"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`$out` replaces wholesale; `$merge` updates incrementally",
            "Rollups run on a schedule with no full rebuild",
            "The output collection is indexable and queryable directly"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "When To Precompute",
          "text": "If a value is read far more often than its inputs change, compute it once and store it."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Attribute Pattern",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ specs: [ { k: 'ram', v: '16GB' },",
            "           { k: 'wt', v: '1.2kg' } ] }",
            "db.p.createIndex({'specs.k':1,'specs.v':1})"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Computed & Extended Reference",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One index then covers every attribute",
            "For hundreds of sparse, variable fields",
            "Product specs, film release dates per country"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Shape Handling",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Polymorphic: different entity shapes, one collection",
            "A type discriminator keeps single-collection queries alive",
            "Schema versioning: `schema_version` on every document",
            "App reads all versions and migrates lazily on write"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Rare And Expensive",
          "items": [
            "Outlier: the celebrity with 10M followers",
            "Flag `has_extras: true`, spill into overflow docs",
            "Approximation: `$inc` by N with probability 1/N",
            "Exactness traded for a huge write reduction"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Hierarchies",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "tree",
          "spec": {
            "root": "Tree models",
            "branches": [
              {
                "label": "parent ref",
                "children": [
                  "cheap writes"
                ]
              },
              {
                "label": "child refs",
                "children": [
                  "fast children"
                ]
              },
              {
                "label": "ancestors",
                "children": [
                  "subtree query"
                ]
              },
              {
                "label": "materialized path",
                "children": [
                  "regex prefix"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Nested sets exist too — each favors a different query",
            "`find({ ancestors: nodeId })` = all descendants, indexed",
            "Path stores `'Books,Programming,Databases'`",
            "Subtree: `find({ path: /^Books,Programming/ })`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Legacy And Housekeeping"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Preallocation: build the full array shape up front (31 days)",
            "Mostly legacy — it mattered under MMAPv1",
            "Document versioning: current here, revisions in a history collection",
            "History docs carry a `revision` field"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Single-Collection Pattern",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Co-locate related entity types via a shared partition field",
            "One index and one query then serve a whole aggregate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Picking One",
          "text": "Pattern selection is driven by the read query, always. Name the query first, then choose the pattern that makes it one indexed lookup."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Unbounded Arrays",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The number one anti-pattern — arrays that grow forever",
            "Ends at 16 MB; each `$push` rewrites the whole document",
            "Signs: swelling docs, multikey bloat, creeping write latency",
            "Never use an array as a queue or log in a hot doc"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Three Ways Out",
          "text": "Reference the children, bucket them, or cap the inline array with `$push` plus `$slice` (subset pattern)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "More Patterns Worth Knowing",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Too Many Collections",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Thousands of collections: storage overhead, slow startup",
            "Each index costs at least ~4 KB plus memory",
            "Collapse with the polymorphic or single-collection pattern"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Bloated Documents"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Fetching a 2 MB doc to read one field wastes cache",
            "Working set stops fitting RAM and reads go to disk",
            "Split cold fields to a side collection on the same `_id`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Index Hygiene",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every index slows writes and eats RAM",
            "`$indexStats` finds the ones nobody uses — drop them",
            "Missing index on a hot query is the other half",
            "Watch `totalDocsExamined` >> `nReturned`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.c.aggregate([{ $indexStats: {} }])",
            "db.c.find(q).explain('executionStats')",
            "// COLLSCAN in winningPlan = no index used"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Case-Insensitive Traps",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Regex case folding is unindexable in general",
            "Use a collation with `strength: 2`",
            "Or store a normalized lowercase field and index that"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.c.createIndex({ name_lower: 1 })",
            "// or a collation with strength: 2",
            "db.c.find({ name_lower: 'ada' })"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Ported Relational Habits"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Mirroring tables 1:1 into collections is the classic porting error",
            "It separates data that is always accessed together",
            "Repeated `$lookup` in a hot path is a schema problem",
            "That path wanted embedding or an extended reference"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Shard key",
            "Failure"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`ObjectId` / time",
              "all inserts hit one chunk"
            ],
            [
              "low cardinality",
              "jumbo chunks, balancer stuck"
            ],
            [
              "do instead",
              "hashed or compound key"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Binaries Belong Elsewhere",
          "items": [
            "Large blobs inside documents wreck the working set",
            "Object storage plus a URL field on the doc",
            "GridFS only when the database must hold the bytes"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Symptom To Fix",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Symptom",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "unbounded array",
              "reference or bucket"
            ],
            [
              "2 MB document",
              "split cold fields"
            ],
            [
              "unused index",
              "`$indexStats`, drop"
            ],
            [
              "COLLSCAN",
              "index the predicate"
            ],
            [
              "hot chunk",
              "hashed shard key"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Master Trade",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "compare",
          "spec": {
            "left": {
              "title": "Embedding buys",
              "items": [
                "read speed",
                "single-doc atomicity",
                "one round trip"
              ]
            },
            "right": {
              "title": "Referencing buys",
              "items": [
                "write efficiency",
                "consistency",
                "bounded doc size"
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Anti-Patterns That Bite",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Duplication is a deliberate tool, not a mistake",
            "Only question: does the copied field change often enough to hurt?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Consistency Ladder",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "single-doc atomic",
              "transaction",
              "change stream",
              "nightly job"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Left is correct and free; right is stalest and cheapest",
            "Transactions: 60 s default, cache pressure from held snapshots",
            "Retry logic for `TransientTransactionError` is mandatory"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Picking A Rung",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Single-document update: atomic, free, always first choice",
            "Change stream: eventual, cheap, resumable after a crash",
            "Nightly job: stalest rung, cheapest to operate",
            "Climb only when the correctness need is real"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Transaction Checklist",
          "items": [
            "Retry on `TransientTransactionError`",
            "Keep the body under 60 s",
            "Small snapshots — the cache is shared",
            "Ask first: could one document do it?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Measure, Do Not Guess",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.c.find(q).explain('executionStats')",
            "// nReturned, totalKeysExamined,",
            "// totalDocsExamined, executionTimeMillis"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Reading",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "keys ≈ docs ≈ returned",
              "index doing its job"
            ],
            [
              "keys >> returned",
              "scanning waste"
            ],
            [
              "docs examined = 0",
              "covered query, fastest"
            ],
            [
              "`COLLSCAN` stage",
              "no usable index"
            ],
            [
              "time up, count flat",
              "working set left RAM"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Worked Example: Slow Feed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.posts.find({user_id:u}).sort({t:-1})",
            "// before: COLLSCAN, 240k docs, 1.9 s",
            "db.posts.createIndex({user_id:1, t:-1})",
            "// after: 20 keys, 20 docs, 3 ms"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "ESR again: equality `user_id`, then sort `t`",
            "`nReturned` never moved — examined work collapsed",
            "Same query text; only the plan changed"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Read The Plan Top Down",
          "text": "`winningPlan` running `IXSCAN` then `FETCH` is healthy. A bare `COLLSCAN`, or a `SORT` stage with no index behind it, is the bill you are paying."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Trade-offs, Validation & Summary",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Covered query = every needed field lives in the index",
            "`$collStats` and `db.collection.stats()` for size truth",
            "Atlas Performance Advisor flags anti-patterns before users do"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Covering A Query",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.c.createIndex({ status: 1, name: 1 })",
            "db.c.find({status:'A'},{_id:0,name:1})",
            "// totalDocsExamined: 0 = covered"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "How do I know the model is wrong?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "`totalDocsExamined` >> `nReturned` on a hot query",
            "Repeated `$lookup` just to paint one screen",
            "Average document size climbing month over month"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Sizing A Collection",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.orders.stats().avgObjSize // 1.9 KB",
            "db.orders.aggregate([{ $collStats:",
            "  { storageStats: {} } }])",
            "// index bytes vs RAM = thrash check"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Average doc size climbing = the model is drifting",
            "Total index size over RAM = thrashing ahead",
            "Record both numbers every release"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Locking The Shape",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Add `$jsonSchema` validation once the model stabilizes",
            "Evolve with `schema_version` — no big-bang migration"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Migrate Without Downtime",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "if (doc.schema_version < 3) upgrade(doc)",
            "// app reads old, writes new — lazily",
            "db.c.find({schema_version:{$lt:3}}).count()"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Backfill The Tail",
          "text": "Lazy migration never reaches cold documents. Sweep the stragglers with a batched job once that count stops falling."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Per-Collection Sizing",
          "items": [
            "Expected doc count and average doc size",
            "Array growth ceiling",
            "Top queries and read/write ratio",
            "Full index list"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Workflow: list queries, map relationships and cardinality",
            "Apply patterns, model it, review against the anti-patterns"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Copied field",
            "Verdict"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`name`",
              "safe, low churn"
            ],
            [
              "`city`",
              "safe, low churn"
            ],
            [
              "`balance`",
              "never copy"
            ],
            [
              "`last_login`",
              "never copy"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Situation",
            "Move"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "few, always together",
              "embed"
            ],
            [
              "many, queried alone",
              "reference"
            ],
            [
              "squillions",
              "parent-ref + bucket + TTL"
            ],
            [
              "hot derived value",
              "compute and store"
            ],
            [
              "unbounded array",
              "bucket + TTL"
            ],
            [
              "display-only field",
              "extended reference"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Five Rules To Keep",
          "text": "Store together what is read together. Bound every array. Index every foreign key. Precompute what is read hot. Let the query plan judge, not intuition."
        }
      ]
    }
